# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationReBootstrap. Reproduces production before #4675 (the fix
# for #4549): a full re-bootstrap installed no drop floor, so a third cluster's
# write the source had applied, deleted and reaped, still on its way to the
# receiver, lands after the export and resurrects the key there.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceNoBootstrapFloor
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the re-bootstrap installs no drop floor, so a third origin's write still in flight resurrects a key the source deleted and reaped
PERTURBS: BeginExport
BOUNDS: Third = TRUE, MaxWrites = 2, Reattach = FALSE

--- FIND
       ELSE /\ fl' = [o \in Thirds |-> SrcLwm(o)]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no drop floor.
       ELSE /\ fl' = [o \in Thirds |-> 0]
--- END
